Subject: [PATCH] android mediacodec encode: set level for OMX codecs when profile is set

ACodec (OMX path) returns INVALID_OPERATION from configure when
"profile" is set without "level". hwcodec always sets the H.264/HEVC
profile but never the level, so hardware encoding fails on OMX-only
devices (e.g. OMX.rk.video_encoder.avc on Android 11, OMX.qcom on 7.1)
and RustDesk falls back to half-scaled software encoding.
---
diff --git a/libavcodec/mediacodecenc.c b/libavcodec/mediacodecenc.c
index 768c815..dbd67ba 100644
--- a/libavcodec/mediacodecenc.c
+++ b/libavcodec/mediacodecenc.c
@@ -342,6 +342,14 @@ static av_cold int mediacodec_init(AVCodecContext *avctx)
     if (ret > 0) {
         av_log(avctx, AV_LOG_DEBUG, "set profile to 0x%x\n", ret);
         ff_AMediaFormat_setInt32(format, "profile", ret);
+        // OMX codecs (ACodec) fail to configure with a profile but no level
+        // (INVALID_OPERATION), e.g. OMX.rk.video_encoder.avc on Android 11.
+        if (s->level <= 0 && s->name && av_strstart(s->name, "OMX.", NULL)) {
+            if (avctx->codec_id == AV_CODEC_ID_H264)
+                s->level = 0x8000;  // AVCLevel51
+            else if (avctx->codec_id == AV_CODEC_ID_HEVC)
+                s->level = 0x10000; // HEVCMainTierLevel51
+        }
     }
     if (s->level > 0) {
         av_log(avctx, AV_LOG_DEBUG, "set level to 0x%x\n", s->level);
